        },
        {
            "name": "John Golden",
            "bio": "John Lionel Golden (1874–1955), born in New York City, was an actor, songwriter, author, and theatrical producer in the United States. As a songwriter, he is most notable as lyricist for \"Poor Butterfly\" (1916). He produced many Broadway shows and four films.",
            "website": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Golden",
